# PostgreSQL — required. schema.prisma's datasource provider is
# "postgresql"; a SQLite file won't work (see PROGRESS.md for why: Vercel's
# serverless functions run on a read-only filesystem, so `file:./dev.db`
# can never persist writes in production — this isn't a SQLite limitation
# specifically, it's true of any file-based database on that platform).
#
# For local development, point this at either:
#   - a local Postgres instance you run yourself (Postgres.app, Docker,
#     native install, etc.) — e.g. postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/amazonw
#   - a Neon development/preview branch (recommended if the production
#     database is already on Neon — keep dev data separate from prod by
#     using a separate branch, not the same database)
#
# Production (Vercel) should point this at the real Neon (or other managed
# Postgres) production database, set as an environment variable in the
# Vercel project settings — never committed here or anywhere in the repo.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@host:5432/dbname?sslmode=require"

# Secret used to sign session cookies (see src/lib/auth.ts). The app throws
# a clear error at request time if this is unset — there is no insecure
# fallback. Generate a real value for any real deployment, e.g.:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
# Never reuse the value below (or any value committed anywhere) in
# production — treat it exactly like a password.
SESSION_SECRET="replace-with-a-random-secret-for-production"
